Git as Single Source of Truth

✨ Hello DevOps Learners!
Continuing my GitOps learning journey after completing Ansible, today I’m exploring an important GitOps concept: Git as the Single Source of Truth. 🚀
This idea is one of the foundations of GitOps and plays a critical role in reliable and automated infrastructure management.

🔹 Config Stored in Git
 In GitOps, all infrastructure and application configurations are stored in Git repositories.
Kubernetes manifests
Deployment YAML files
Infrastructure configurations
This means the entire system state is defined in Git.

🔹 Version History Benefits
 Since everything is stored in Git:
Every change is tracked and auditable
Teams can see who changed what and when
Configuration changes are reviewed through pull requests
This improves collaboration and prevents unexpected changes.

🔹 Rollback Using Git
 If something goes wrong in production:
Simply revert to a previous Git commit
GitOps tools automatically sync the system back to that version
This makes rollbacks fast, safe, and reliable compared to manual fixes.

💡 Key Insight:
 When Git becomes the source of truth, infrastructure becomes predictable, transparent, and easy to manage.
